        "story": "\"I gotta change the rep us HR guys have.\" My smile isn't that forced. \"Thanks.\" Finally, he walks away, leaving me alone with an hour of work still to go and a dozen eyes burning against my back. I need to plot my revenge on everyone. Because this has sparked joy in their hearts. The thing about working in a regional office for a big-box retailer that sells corn by-products, camping things, and cream for various types of rashes and boils is that not one of us is living our dream. They'll talk about starting a sandwich truck, even though they aren't even qualified to roast a marshmallow, or fleeing to Belize to teach surfing lessons. But every one of them shows up on Monday, until the weeks turn into a life sentence. My situation is the only beauty left in life for them.",
        "story_cn": "“得扭转外界对咱们HR的刻板印象了。”我的笑容还算自然。“多谢。”他终于走开，留我独自面对一小时未竟的工作，以及数十道灼烧后背的视线。我得谋划场复仇大戏，因为我的窘态正是他们的快乐源泉。在这家售卖玉米副产品、露营装备和各式皮疹药膏的大型零售企业区域办事处工作，没有谁真正在追逐梦想。他们谈论着要开流动三明治车——尽管连棉花糖都烧不成炭；或是逃往伯利兹教授冲浪——但每个人都准时在周一现身，直到数周堆叠成终生苦役。而我的处境，已是他们黯淡生活里仅存的风景。",
