        "beatId": 1,
        "story": "I stare down the scratched-up door to our office floor, willing myself to open it. Each dent tells the story of someone knocking it with the paper cart on a different version of the same old day. My hand is heavy as I pull the handle and drag myself into the sterile air that hasn't seen the light of day. As I make my way to my desk, nobody looks up. The drone of the computer fans matches the blank stares the humans give the machines in return. I'm invisible, until Rhonda's gaze drifts to me -- it's just a small nod, but that's more than I usually get. I give her a small grin in return. Armin is zoning out, presumably still working on the same accounting grids he's been staring at but hasn't altered in a significant way for days.",
        "story_cn": "我盯着办公室楼层那扇布满刮痕的门，逼迫自己推开它。每一道凹痕都诉说着某个同样乏味的日子里，某人推着纸箱车撞门的旧事。当我握住门把手将自己拖进那从未见过日光的无菌空气时，手臂沉重如铅。走向工位的路上无人抬头，电脑风扇的嗡鸣与人类投向机器的空洞眼神形成共振。我本是隐形人，直到朗达的目光飘来——只是个轻微颔首，却已超过平日所得。我回以一个腼腆笑容。阿尔敏正神游天外，八成还在捣鼓那些他已盯了数日却未见实质改动的会计表格。",
