        "story": "I throw on a hoodie that I hope covers both my slept-in hair situation and my lost dignity, pile my garbage into the bin, throw the gin bottle and glass under the sink, and do a quick scan to make sure there are no obvious signs that the human embodiment of a bag of merde lives here. There's an empty chip bag on the coffee table, and an old take-out container that still has broth and pieces of wonton wrapper in it on the counter, but other than that, I should be able to get away with medium complaints. I shovel both pieces of garbage into a random cupboard since the bin is full and brace myself. I barely open the door. \"What brings you here?\" Mom barrels past me with a Tupperware container so huge, she had to have gotten it from a specialty store. \"No need to heat this up if you get plates.\" I should've known this was coming. Every now and then, she shows up with food without warning. I'm sure it's to try to keep me living under a similar regimen as when I was home, like I pretend to be, but unfortunately for us both, shit has veered incredibly off track.",
        "story_cn": "我抓起连帽衫——但愿能遮住睡塌的发型与尽失的颜面，把垃圾堆进桶里，将金酒瓶与杯子塞到水槽下，迅速扫视确保没有\"人形垃圾袋居住于此\"的明显痕迹。咖啡桌上有空薯片袋，台面还摆着剩汤与馄饨皮的旧外卖盒，除此之外，勉强能逃过严厉指责。我把两袋垃圾铲进任意橱柜——垃圾桶已满，然后屏息凝神。刚把门拉开条缝：\"什么风把您吹来了？\"母亲挤开我冲进来，抱着特大号保鲜盒，非专业超市买不到的那种。\"要是有盘子就不用加热。\"早该料到。她总突然带食物上门。准是想让我继续过家里那套生活——就像我假装还在过的那样。可惜对我们俩而言，生活早偏航得面目全非。",
