        "beatId": 9,
        "story": "It's like you don't care.\" She says this with all the severity of a doctor making a deadly diagnosis. \"Are you okay?\" The crease in her brow -- I hate that crease, critical and concerned all at once. I need to curl into a ball. I scramble for some excuse to make it go away. \"The problem is that I care too much and don't know where to start.\" She fake slaps the space between us in a dismissive gesture, her acrylic nails cutting the air like little claws. \"Get on with you. It's very serious to be this bad.\" And to prove her point, she wipes the cloth under a windowsill that I'm pretty sure nobody has ever cleaned in the history of this apartment's construction. \"This dust is from long time ago.\" She hardens her gaze accusingly, and I stiffen -- she is not done with me yet.",
        "story_cn": "“简直像你根本不在乎。”她说这话的神态，堪比医生宣判绝症般冷酷。“你还好吗？”她眉间的褶皱——我憎恶那道兼具苛责与关切的褶皱。我只想蜷缩成团。慌忙搜寻借口想抹去这神情。“问题是我太在乎，却不知从何开始。”她虚挥一掌拂过我们之间的空气，那姿态仿佛掸开什么脏东西，亚克力指甲在空中划出利爪般的弧度。“得了吧，把事情搞砸到这种地步才严重呢。”为印证此言，她竟抹向窗台下沿——我敢打赌这处积灰自这公寓建造以来从未被清理过。“这灰尘是陈年旧物。”她目光骤冷如指控，我浑身僵直——她还没打算放过我。",
