        "beatId": 16,
        "story": "She's never one to deny an easy answer when it is gifted to her. \"Make sure you finish the bowl. It's very healthy.\" I smile and take another hefty spoonful of the ashe reshteh, letting the comforting, familiar flavors wash through me. \"I'll put the rest in the fridge.\" Once Mom gathers everything, including Dad and his iPad, she turns to me and whispers, \"The girl with the dirty fingernails that let us in is still outside. Should we call her mom?\" Oh god. I peer out the window and see Miley's mousy head leaning against the wall in the hallway. \"Don't worry about her. That's normal.\" But as soon as I say it, she shifts, sinking lower -- she's just sitting there by herself?",
        "story_cn": "她向来懂得顺手接住送上门的台阶。“记得把这碗吃光，可有营养了。”我微笑着又舀起一大勺波斯蔬菜浓汤，任那熟悉温厚的滋味在唇齿间漫开。“剩下的我放冰箱。”待母亲收拾好所有碗碟，连同抱着平板的父亲一同劝离后，她转身对我低语：“刚才给我们开门的那个指甲脏兮兮的女孩还在外头。要叫她妈妈来接吗？”天哪。我探向窗外，看见米莉灰扑扑的脑袋正倚在走廊墙边。“别管她，小孩子都这样。”可话音刚落，她身子一歪，顺着墙根滑坐下去——她竟独自坐在那儿？",
