        "story": "\"Now that sounds like you.\" But there's still some tension creasing at the corners of his eyes. How can he read me so well, so often? My eyes dart again to the maroon folder sitting on his desk, and I think of that little note again: help her feel safe. I hear myself say, \"I don't really like who I was back then.\" I instantly regret my words. It's far too close to the bone. But Cliff nods and leans an inch closer across the desk. \"Well, I don't know what you were like then -- aside from that you grew up dreaming of working at Supershops, of course -- but the Jolene of now is pretty great.\" His words are like a warm blanket. It's not much, but it still feels like a small piece of the weight on my shoulders has been lifted.",
        "story_cn": "“这语气才像你。”但他眼角的褶皱里仍有一丝紧绷。他为何总能如此轻易、如此频繁地看穿我？我的目光再次瞟向他桌上那个栗色的文件夹，那张小纸条上的字句又浮现脑海：让她感到安全。我听见自己说：“我不太喜欢那时候的自己。”话音刚落便已后悔，那未免太戳心了。但克里夫点了点头，隔着办公桌朝这边倾近了一英寸。“嗯，我不知道你过去怎样——除了你从小梦想在‘超级商店’工作，这点当然知道——但现在的乔琳相当出色。”他的话语像一条温暖的毛毯。虽只是轻言片语，肩上那沉甸甸的负担，却仿佛真的卸下了一小块。",
