        "story": "\"He's always been like that. Even when we were kids, he'd save me his cookies from the government lunch program. Can you imagine that? I like to tell him he's being a bitchy martyr, for balance.\" My smile is wobbly. I like her, and -- another rush piles through my abdomen, heavier than the last -- I like Cliff. Cliff returns with a giant tray piled high with steaming food that's been through every kind of processing invented. \"There's three more trays, so hold tight,\" he says as he heads back to the counter. He leaves me alone with a giant pile of French fries.",
