        "story": "\"Okay,\" Cliff echoes. \"Meet you in the parkade after work.\" He heads back into the hall, where the procession of Larry handlers just were. Stu is already wheeling Larry's chair across the floor. The energy in the room is a vibrant hum. Everyone is still whispering to each other, but the excitement that was previously peppering their voices has faded into insecurity. Larry's display wasn't just about him. Nobody is immune to thinking they might be wasting their only life on a place that can toss you out without a second thought. This will be a reminder to anyone who ever suspected a company gave a shit about them.",
        "story_cn": "“好的，”克里夫附和道。“下班后停车场见。”他转身走回走廊——刚才那队拉里的助理们就在那里。斯图已经推着拉里的轮椅穿过地板。房间里的气氛震颤着嗡鸣。人人仍在窃窃私语，但先前声音里夹杂的兴奋早已褪成不安。拉里的爆发不仅仅关乎他自身。无人能豁免那种念头：自己或许正将唯一的生命耗在一个可以毫不犹豫将你抛弃的地方。这对每个曾以为公司会在乎自己的人，都是个提醒。",
