        "story": "The interesting slash depressing thing about working for a corporation that's been around for as long as Supershops has is that a lot of things that are obvious wastes of time and money have most certainly happened. In my deep dive of the company database, I've learned that between the years 2004 and 2013, the office had a \"newspaper.\" It was literally a weekly periodical about the people here and the things they did. There's a notice about the formation of the office Coffee Club (decades old, who would have thought!), an article about the office-wide switch to Windows Vista, and a write-up of a Bring Your Child to Work Day, featuring an old picture of Rhonda with a young child hugging her waist, who the caption confirms is Carl. I stare at their beaming smiles for several seconds, every muscle in my body as heavy as lead. Gregory was featured in this newspaper three times. The first was on January 4, 2005, when Gregory launched a new motivational contest for the office employees. I could've used this, but Larry D. Goodwin won, and the picture is of Gregory handing him a laminated certificate.",
        "story_cn": "在超商店这样历史悠久的公司工作，有趣又憋屈的是，那些明显浪费时间和金钱的事，肯定都真实发生过。我在深挖公司数据库时发现，2004到2013年间，办公室竟有份“报纸”——字面意义上的周刊，记录这里的人和事。上面有办公室“咖啡俱乐部”成立的告示（几十年历史了，谁能想到！），有关于全员切换Windows Vista系统的报道，还有“带孩子上班日”的专题，配着朗达的老照片——一个小孩搂着她腰，图注证实那是卡尔。我盯着他们灿烂的笑容看了几秒，身体每块肌肉都沉得像铅。格雷戈里在这份报上出现过三次：第一次是2005年1月4日，他为员工发起了新激励竞赛。我本该学学这招，但拉里·D·古德温赢了，照片里格雷戈里正递给他塑封的证书。",
