        "story": "It's time to make my exit. But as soon as I open the stall's door, I curse the universe for its terrible timing. The bathroom door swings open and in walks Caitlin. She walks right past my ajar stall and stands in front of the mirror, checking herself. And holy shit, she hasn't noticed me. \"Oh, you're so lucky,\" she says to her reflection, voice slurred. \"You're going to have so much good stuff. You're perfect.\" This would normally be a blessed, magical occasion, and I'd enjoy this image for decades, but the door I'm still holding half open creaks, and Caitlin whips around, locking her eyes on me -- as best she can.",
