        "beatId": 1,
        "story": "I've compiled an embarrassing amount of recycling after finishing the last of my apartment clear-out. It took me four whole days, but I'll never get off track again, maybe. It's when I'm gathering all the old mail -- some realtor flyers from those delusional enough to send them to us and menus from restaurants that seem heartbreakingly desperate -- that I spot the letters Cliff left, and my stomach flips. I pick the first one up and recognize Rhonda's handwriting immediately. Honey, First, I'm sorry about the way things happened on your last day. When I heard the mutterings you'd been spying on us, I was so miffed. I had some big secrets you were seeing and that wasn't okay. But one thing I'm good at is forgiveness and understanding desperate situations.",
        "story_cn": "收拾完公寓最后一点杂物后，我囤积的废品多到令人难堪。整整耗了四天，但也许，这次我再也不会把事情搞砸了。当我整理那些旧信件——来自某些妄想症患者投递的房产传单，还有那些餐馆菜单，每一张都透着令人心酸的绝望——我瞥见了克里夫留下的那些信，心头一沉。我拿起第一封，立刻认出了朗达的笔迹。亲爱的，首先，为你最后那天发生的事，我很抱歉。听说有传言你在监视我们时，我气坏了。我当时正藏着些见不得光的大秘密，这可不行。不过，有一件事我很擅长，那就是原谅，也懂得体谅走投无路的处境。",
